==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_AssignmentMatchesStatus  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_AssignmentMatchesStatus.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact breaks the Submitted-iff-unassigned coupling; injecting an Approved application with no assigned officer produces an instance the queue-shape predicate must reject.
    expected to FAIL: FR_010_UnassignedQueueShape
      - FR_010_UnassignedQueueShape: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_DecisionByAssignedOfficer  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_DecisionByAssignedOfficer.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact lets the model invent a decision whose decider differs from the application's assigned officer, which is exactly the bug FR-013 forbids.
    expected to FAIL: FR_013_OnlyAssignedOfficerDecides
      - FR_013_OnlyAssignedOfficerDecides: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_SuccessRequiresPermission  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_SuccessRequiresPermission.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact disconnects the permission matrix from Operation outcomes; injecting a successful customer claim (which the matrix denies) forces a counterexample that LeastPrivilege must catch.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_002_CustomerScope
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_002_CustomerScope: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_DecisionReasonNonEmpty  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_DecisionReasonNonEmpty.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact allows a Decision row with an empty reason to be persisted, which FR-014 says must never happen even structurally.
    expected to FAIL: FR_014_NonEmptyReason, ValidationBeforeMutation
      - FR_014_NonEmptyReason: FAIL (expected)
      - ValidationBeforeMutation: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_InitialSubmissionEvent  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_InitialSubmissionEvent.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact lets the model omit the (none)->Submitted audit entry; injecting a LoanApplication with no initial event manifests the FR-009 / AuditCompleteness violation directly.
    expected to FAIL: FR_009_InitialSubmissionAudit, AuditCompleteness
      - FR_009_InitialSubmissionAudit: FAIL (expected)
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_CustomerNonOwnedReturnsNotFound  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_CustomerNonOwnedReturnsNotFound.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact removes the contract that customer access to a non-owned application masquerades as 404; injecting an operation that responds VPermissionDenied instead of VNotFound surfaces the information leak.
    expected to FAIL: NoInformationLeakage, FR_020_OwnershipAndNoLeak
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_020_OwnershipAndNoLeak: FAIL (expected)

